\section{Scientific distinctions}{

The package explicitly distinguishes:
\itemize{
\item rollout-model value: the estimand defined by the rollout continuation
policy, truncation rule, and payoff mapping;
\item proxy reference: a high-budget Monte Carlo estimate used as a practical
reference for regret and ranking diagnostics;
\item true backgammon strength / game-theoretic truth: not available and never
implied by the package outputs.
}

Posterior quantities are therefore approximate and model-relative, not claims
of exact truth.

The package now exposes an explicit reward/posterior model layer. The
default front door is the scalar-payoff baseline
\code{reward_model = "scalar_payoff"} with \code{posterior_model = "beta_pseudo"},
while coherent alternatives such as \code{win_loss + beta_bernoulli} and
\code{categorical_outcome + dirichlet_multinomial} are available for direct
comparison.
}

